1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:00,809
Welcome to Track B.

2
00:00:00,809 --> 00:00:03,447
We start with voice — actually talking to your agent out loud.

3
00:00:03,447 --> 00:00:06,000
In this one we hold a first spoken conversation, end to end.

4
00:00:06,000 --> 00:00:07,687
Press New call at the top of the sidebar.

5
00:00:07,687 --> 00:00:14,765
A call needs two things: hearing — that's Whisper, running locally to turn your speech into text — and speaking, an engine that voices the reply, which is the next episode.

6
00:00:14,765 --> 00:00:16,000
Right now we focus on hearing.

7
00:00:16,000 --> 00:00:19,436
On your very first call, the app downloads a Whisper model — a one-time thing.

8
00:00:19,436 --> 00:00:24,414
You pick the size: tiny is fastest and roughest, small is slowest and most accurate, and base sits in the middle.

9
00:00:24,414 --> 00:00:26,000
Base is a good default; start there.

10
00:00:26,000 --> 00:00:27,128
Three ways to talk to it.

11
00:00:27,128 --> 00:00:30,694
Auto — it listens continuously and replies when you stop; best with headphones.

12
00:00:30,694 --> 00:00:34,667
Push-to-talk — hold Control Shift V, which is global, so it works even from another app.

13
00:00:34,667 --> 00:00:36,969
And Wake word — it waits until you say the trigger.

14
00:00:36,969 --> 00:00:39,000
Pick Auto for a hands-free chat at your desk.

15
00:00:39,000 --> 00:00:46,273
When you end a call, it's saved just like a chat — you'll find it in the sidebar, and reopening it resumes as a call, not a transcript you have to read.

16
00:00:46,273 --> 00:00:49,000
Your spoken conversations are first-class, not throwaway.

17
00:00:49,000 --> 00:00:53,323
One small gotcha, and it's a nice one: if you start a call and never actually say anything, it isn't saved.

18
00:00:53,323 --> 00:00:57,000
A mis-press doesn't leave empty clutter in your sidebar — only real exchanges stick around.

19
00:00:57,000 --> 00:00:58,026
It can hear you now.

20
00:00:58,026 --> 00:01:03,000
Next we give it a voice — comparing the four synthesis engines and landing on a sensible default.

